I've taken a quick stab at organizing the agenda for OEDEM. The only 
thing I feel strongly about is getting the General Assembly over with 
first. The only agenda item for the General Assembly that could be time 
consuming is the online voting procedure.

If anyone has strong feelings on the online voting, it would be good to 
bring a written suggestion. The current system is not perfect, but it 
does work and has been tested so it does not get into situations that 
lead to no clear result. If there are no concrete ideas for the GA to 
discuss, I would suggest that interested parties volunteer to do some 
research into online voting processes and make suggestions.

Please review the agenda and make suggestions. This a meeting for 
everyone to participate in. Emailed thoughts are welcome. I left the 
times flexible after the first couple of items.

Philip

PS: And once again, a big thanks to Intel for arranging for the meeting 
room.


